= Karl Radek

Radek is the Comintern's expert on Germany, a brilliant journalist and an old friend of the party, as well as its most severe critic. He has Zinoviev's ear. He is quick to adapt to whichever course Moscow takes next, which is useful to the party and a warning about it.

